WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.370
JENNY BROWN: Happy
2022, everyone.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.950
It's so good to be back.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.890
Today, we're talking
about starting your year

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.190
with free cloud education,
more inclusive hybrid

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.800
meetings, and the
eight megatrends

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.410
that we're looking at to
improve cloud security

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.210
and cloud adoption.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.450
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.990
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.500
If one of your resolutions
was to grow your cloud skills,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.710
you're in luck.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.580
We've compiled a list of
free learning opportunities

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.370
for you to kick off your
year with education,

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.420
from free access to Cloud Skills
Boost to half-day trainings

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.920
on cloud fundamentals.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.530
Go to the blog for the full
list, dates, and to sign up.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.770
As we enter 2022, it's
clear that adjusting

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.430
to ambiguity and remote
work is critical to success.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.760
Google Meet spent much
of 2021 adding features

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.960
and functionality to Workspace
to support a hybrid team,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.110
from backgrounds to
noise cancellation.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.360
Google also spent
much of last year

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.430
developing our
own best practices

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.550
as a team for making hybrid
meetings as inclusive

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:16.140
as possible to further improve
that hybrid work experience.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.120
Check out the blog
for more details

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.070
on how to make the
most of your meetings.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:24.880
At Google Cloud, we
prioritize security by design

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.660
and work continuously to deliver
secure products and customer

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.860
controls.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.280
Additionally, we take advantage
of industry megatrends

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.590
that increase cloud
security further,

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:39.130
outpacing the security of
on-prem infrastructure.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.770
IT decision makers should
pay close attention

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.630
to these megatrends,
because they're

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:48.430
not just transient issues to be
ignored once 2023 rolls around.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:52.330
They guide the development of
cloud security and technology,

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.870
and will continue to do so
for the foreseeable future.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:00.250
Head to the blog for the
full list and a deep dive.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.910
If you want to read more about
any of these announcements

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.860
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.620
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.669
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:11.990
We'll see you in the cloud.

